# Autosave with a persistent cleanup worker: Commit clones the work tree into a
# private mkdtemp staging (<commit>.swx-save-<pid>.XXXXXX/tree) and swaps it
# atomically with the commit (clone+swap stay synchronous); the swapped-out old
# version is deleted by one QOS_CLASS_BACKGROUND worker (FIFO of 4 plus the one
# being deleted), never by a thread per commit. SWX_SAVE_ASYNC precedes
# DM_SAVE_ASYNC (alias); both absent = on, =0 = synchronous legacy path. A full
# queue or a worker that will not start falls back to a synchronous delete
# outside the mount locks; the commit stays published. Crash orphans of the
# staging are swept at mount only when their PID is provably gone. Covers
# h_fs_Commit and h_fs_CommitList (same engine). See docs/async_writes_evaluation.md.
